From: mscharged-port
Subject: Sort with the Wii's qsort natively
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84
Classification: native libc compatibility

qsort leaves the order of equal elements to the implementation, and the
host libraries disagree: for two equal elements glibc keeps them as they
are, while the Wii's MSL heapsort and Windows' UCRT swap them, and longer
arrays differ further. The online draft sorts the teams by score
(NetworkDraft::CompareDraftTeams), so two new players tie: a Linux and a
Windows machine then each put their own team first, both draft at once and
the match falls out of sync. cTeam::UpdateTeamAI sorts the fielders by
their X position the same way during a match, and cGame orders each
player's closest players by distance with nlQSort.

Natively these calls and nlQSort use ChargedWii_qsort
(src/platform/wii_qsort.h), the MSL qsort of the decomp built under its own
name (cmake/WiiQsort.cmake), so every host sorts as the Wii and as Dolphin.
The friend list, the ranking rows, the fonts and GameSpy's arrays take it
too. The Wii build is unchanged.

diff --git a/include/NL/nlAlgorithm.h b/include/NL/nlAlgorithm.h
index 41349c4..1d2a398 100644
--- a/include/NL/nlAlgorithm.h
+++ b/include/NL/nlAlgorithm.h
@@ -2,6 +2,12 @@
 #define NL_ALGORITHM_H
 
 #include "stdlib.h"
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE)
+// src/platform/wii_qsort.h, declared here so that every includer compiles
+// without the port's include path.
+extern "C" void ChargedWii_qsort(void* base, size_t count, size_t size,
+    int (*compare)(const void*, const void*));
+#endif
 
 template <typename T, typename Key>
 T* nlBSearch(const Key& key, T* array, int size)
@@ -38,7 +44,12 @@ int nlDefaultQSortComparer(const T* pa, const T* pb)
 template <typename T>
 inline void nlQSort(T* array, int count, int (*comparefunc)(const T*, const T*))
 {
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE)
+    // cGame sorts the players by distance with it: ties must fall as on the Wii.
+    ChargedWii_qsort(array, count, sizeof(T), (int (*)(const void*, const void*))comparefunc);
+#else
     qsort(array, count, sizeof(T), (int (*)(const void*, const void*))comparefunc);
+#endif
 }
 
 #endif // NL_ALGORITHM_H
